=== SURVEY ===
Web source AIAutoTripNameSuggestion.tsx = `withAiFeature('auto-trip-naming', InnerSection)`. The
inner section reads the `tripId` prop (its `canStart = !!tripId`), memoises the draft URL
(`tripId ? '/ai/trips/{encoded}/name/draft' : '/ai/trips/0/name/draft'`), opens a `useAiStream`
with an empty `{}` body, and renders an `AIFeatureCard`:
  • title  "Suggest a trip name" (trips.detail.aiSuggestName.title)
  • desc   "Get a short, propose-only name suggestion …" (trips.detail.aiSuggestName.description)
  • button "Suggest a name" (trips.detail.aiSuggestName.generateButton) — surfaced as aria/tooltip;
           the visible CTA is the universal "Ask Helix" / "Helix is thinking…" (helix.askHelix /
           helix.thinking), disabled when `!canStart || streaming`.
  • badge  "Helix" (trips.detail.aiSuggestName.badge)
AIFeatureCard → AiOutputPanel renders: nothing when idle; AIThinkingIndicator (shimmer lines +
dots) while streaming with no text; the streamed proposal text; or "Helix error: {msg}"
(helix.errorLabel / ai.common.errorUnknown). useAiStream lifecycle: idle→streaming→done|error
(+paused-confirm); SSE frames `event:`/`data:`-delimited, parsed by parseSSEFrame/toTypedEvent,
delta-accumulated, terminal done/error with structured limit fields (F9).
Data sources (P1/S8): useTranslation, useAiStream. Shared components: AIFeatureCard, withAiFeature.
Charts/maps: none. Canonical surface pattern studied: shared-surfaces/AnnouncerRegion
(Adapter/Model/Seams/View/Views/States/Previews/strings/Tests/ModelTests).

=== REASONING ===
- The native surface reproduces the web composition as a Helix feature card: a glass panel over a
  header (title + Helix badge + description + canStart empty-hint), the universal Ask Helix button,
  and the streaming output panel, bound through `AITripNameModel` (no HTTP/SSE in the view).
- Architecture mirrors the canonical AnnouncerRegion leaf:
  • Adapter (pure, Foundation): AiStreamLifecycle (web AiStreamState), AiStreamEvent (the union),
    AiLimitInfo (F9), AiStreamSnapshot (useAiStream result), AiStreamReducer (verbatim port of the
    `handleEvent` switch + start/close/cancel/fail transitions), AiSseFrameParser (verbatim port of
    parseSSEFrame + toTypedEvent with the same `typeof` field guards, reproduced via CFBoolean-aware
    JSON scalar helpers), AITripNameEndpoint (the useMemo draft-URL + featureID + slug),
    AITripNameAccessibility.
  • Model: AITripNameTelemetry seam (P1/S11 view.opened) + OSLog default; AITripNameConnection axis;
    AITripNameInput (gate + tripId + connectivity → canStart = web !!tripId, additionally
    offline-gated); AITripNameResolved + Projection (gatedOff/loading/idle/thinking/suggestion/error);
    @Observable AITripNameModel (binds the context source + the stream driver, generate()/cancel()/
    retry()/refresh(), one-shot stale auto-refresh); AITripNameStrings i18n facade.
  • Seams: AITripNameSource protocol (+Live host-binding / InMemory); AITripNameStreamDriver protocol
    (the useAiStream port) with a REAL URLSession.bytes SSE driver (POST {} to
    `${base}/api/v1{path}`, blank-line framing → AiSseFrameParser → AiStreamReducer, http_/cancel/
    close semantics matching the web hook) + an InMemory scripted double.
  • View/Views/States + Previews + strings + Tests/ModelTests.
- The `withAiFeature` gate is reproduced faithfully: when the AI flag is off the surface renders
  NOTHING (ADR-015 AI-Off contract — the gate exists precisely so no AI surface leaks; rendering a
  visible "off" card would violate it). The "never a blank box" P4 rule is honoured for the DATA
  states (loading/idle/thinking/suggestion/error all render real content); idle is a friendly,
  Helix-marked prompt rather than the web's literal empty panel.
- Rejected: porting Tailwind/HelixMark SVG literally (drew a native double-helix Shape + used the
  P1/S9 tokens); decoding SSE data with one all-fields Codable struct (an irrelevant wrong-typed
  field would wrongly invalidate a valid frame — used a loose dict + per-field `typeof` guards to
  match the web parser exactly; asserted by testDeltaIgnoresIrrelevantWrongTypedField); HTTP in the
  view (routed through the driver seam); a cancel-on-tap button (web button is disabled while
  streaming — matched).

